# Target C-II — strict aggregate gap forces component remainder

**Date:** 2026-09-13  
**Status:** proof-only Type-II composition; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

This note composes the proof-only strict aggregate moment gap with the audited-working
§§160--161 remainder identity. It gives a finite identity and an asymptotic branch
split that were not retained in the earlier detour note.

Put

\[
S_D:=\sum_r d_r,\qquad
X_D:=q-k-S_D,
\qquad
G_D:=2+q+m-k-S_D,
\]

where `m` is the number of nonunit loaded-hull sides and `k=d_H+s_Z`. The
proof-only strict aggregate result gives

\[
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{X_D\over D}
\ge
\alpha,
\qquad
\alpha:={\pi\over20}(2-\sqrt3)
=0.0420893607\ldots .
\tag{SGR.1}
\]

The audited §160 identity is

\[
G_D=R_I+s_B+\sum_r(\delta_r+2-d_r)\ge0.
\tag{SGR.2}
\]

The new consequence is

\[
\boxed{G_D=m+2+X_D,}
\tag{SGR.3}
\]

and therefore

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{G_D-m\over D}\ge\alpha.
}
\tag{SGR.4}
\]

Thus the aggregate detour floor cannot be paid while both the nonunit loaded-hull
side count and the §160 component remainder are sublinear.

## 1. Exact identity

Substitute the definitions of `X_D` and `G_D`:

\[
G_D-(m+2+X_D)
=2+q+m-k-S_D-m-2-(q-k-S_D)=0.
\]

This is finite and has no limiting or injectivity assumption. Combining it with
(SGR.1) gives (SGR.4). Since the audited §160 decomposition has nonnegative terms,
the same conclusion applies to the actual remainder `R_I+s_B+sum_r eta_r`, not to
an auxiliary signed quantity.

## 2. Transfer to the long-side correction

Let

\[
\chi_D:=q+m-\operatorname{per}(F),
\qquad
\delta_D:={b-\operatorname{per}(F)\over D}.
\]

The exact §172 identity is

\[
\chi_D=S_D+G_D+k-\operatorname{per}(F)-2,
\qquad
b-\operatorname{per}(F)=u_B+\chi_D,
\tag{SGR.5}
\]

with `u_B>=0`. Along any Type-II subsequence for which

\[
{S_D\over D}\to S,
\qquad {m\over D}\to\mu,
\qquad {k\over D}\to\kappa,
\]

the Type-II perimeter limit and (SGR.4) imply

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\chi_D\over D}
\ge S+\mu+\kappa+\alpha-\pi.
}
\tag{SGR.6}
\]

Consequently the actual outer-walk detour obeys the branch-safe bound

\[
\boxed{
\liminf \delta_D
\ge\bigl(S+\mu+\kappa+\alpha-\pi\bigr)_+.
}
\tag{SGR.7}
\]

No sign is assigned to `chi_D` when the displayed lower bound is negative. The
positive-part step uses only `b>=per(F)` and `u_B>=0`.

## 3. Scoped endpoint consequence

On the proof-only Section-118 common-cap profile, the prior audited moment bound is

\[
S\ge S_{118}:=2.798596312209462\ldots .
\]

Hence every subsequence in that same profile satisfies

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\chi_D\over D}
\ge {m\over D}+{k\over D}-0.3009069810\ldots-o(1),
}
\tag{SGR.8}
\]

and

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {b-\operatorname{per}(F)\over D}
\ge
\left({m\over D}+{k\over D}-0.3009069810\ldots\right)_+-o(1).
}
\tag{SGR.9}
\]

For example, if `m+k >= (0.300907+epsilon)D` along a common subsequence, then the
old outer contact walk has at least `epsilon D-o(D)` excess over the force-hull
perimeter. This is a genuine source-level dichotomy: a negative long-side correction
is possible only below the explicit `m+k` threshold, and above that threshold the
outer detour is forced.

The earlier §172 carrier-area bound remains available simultaneously. On its
Section-118 data it gives `chi_D/D >= -0.1036221+k/D-o(1)`. Taking the larger of
that bound and (SGR.8) is valid, but does not remove the low-`m` branch.

## 4. Interaction with the exact hull ledger

In Type II, `e_BB=q-m` and the audited loaded-hull identity is

\[
e_{BB}=Q+2k+u_B.
\tag{SGR.10}
\]

Using `Q/D=2(q-k)/D-\pi-\delta_D+o(1)` gives the finite/asymptotic compatibility
inequality

\[
{m\over D}+{k\over D}
\le
\pi+\delta_D-{q-k\over D}+o(1).
\tag{SGR.11}
\]

Thus a proposed closure of the low-`m` branch must control the remaining
`q-k`/outer-detour tradeoff; (SGR.7) alone does not provide that control.

## 5. Scope and classification

- (SGR.3)--(SGR.4) are exact/one-line consequences of the proof-only strict gap and
  audited §160; the theorem state is unchanged.
- (SGR.6)--(SGR.9) use the audited §172 identities and the same-subsequence
  Section-118 profile. No independent carrier optimization is made.
- Contact-isolated source points remain outside the core affine-kernel statement.
- No KKT coefficient floor, global two-phase assumption, strict diameter descent, or
  exact unit triangle is asserted.

**Classification:** proved candidate awaiting hostile audit; proof-only Type-II
composition. C-II remains open.
